The approach uses a Map to track pending promises keyed by the loader argument. When `load(key)` is called, if a promise for that key already exists and hasn’t settled yet, we return it directly so all callers share the same promise. Once the promise settles (fulfills or rejects), we delete it from the Map so subsequent calls with the same key trigger a fresh loader invocation. We increment `inflight` when starting a new load and decrement it on settlement, handling both fulfillment and rejection to ensure rejections aren’t cached.

