hjs-008.text:
My approach is to implement a tagged template function `sqlTag` that processes the template literal parts and interpolations. For each interpolation, if it's a plain value (not an object with `text` and `values`), it becomes a placeholder `$n`. If the interpolation is itself an object returned by `sqlTag`, we inline its SQL text and adjust placeholder indices to maintain global numbering. If the interpolation is an array, we generate a parenthesized list of placeholders (e.g., `($1,$2)`), with each array element getting its own placeholder. We track the current placeholder index globally within the call and increment it per interpolation. Edge cases include empty arrays (resulting in `()`, which may need special handling but per spec we just produce placeholders), nested arrays, and ensuring renumbering of inlined SQL works correctly even when multiple levels of nesting occur.

ANSWER:
```javascript
function sqlTag(strings, ...interpolations) {
  let text = '';
  let values = [];
  let placeholderIndex = 1;

  for (let i = 0; i < strings.length; i++) {
    text += strings[i];
    if (i < interpolations.length) {
      const val = interpolations[i];
      if (Array.isArray(val)) {
        const placeholders = [];
        for (let j = 0; j < val.length; j++) {
          placeholders.push(`$${placeholderIndex}`);
          values.push(val[j]);
          placeholderIndex++;
        }
        text += `(${placeholders.join(',')})`;
      } else if (val && typeof val === 'object' && Array.isArray(val.values) && typeof val.text === 'string') {
        // Inlined SQL object
        const inlinedText = val.text.replace(/\$(\d+)/g, (_, num) => {
          const offset = parseInt(num, 10);
          return `$${offset + placeholderIndex - 1}`;
        });
        text += inlinedText;
        values = values.concat(val.values.map(() => {
          placeholderIndex++;
          return null; // dummy, actual value will be pushed separately
        }));
        for (let j = 0; j < val.values.length; j++) {
          values[values.length - val.values.length + j] = val.values[j];
        }
      } else {
        text += `$${placeholderIndex}`;
        values.push(val);
        placeholderIndex++;
      }
    }
  }

  return { text, values };
}

module.exports = sqlTag;
```

