I'll implement a type-safe route definition system using TypeScript's template literal types and conditional types to extract parameter names from path templates. The approach will involve:  
1) Parsing the route paths at compile time using template literal inference to capture `:paramName` segments  
2) Using mapped types and generics to ensure the returned functions accept only the exact params required for each route  
3) Handling edge cases like empty params (no `:name` segments), duplicate param names in a single path, and ensuring the interpolation function returns a properly typed string  

The implementation will use a generic `DefineRoutes` type that maps each route name to its path template, then constructs a corresponding object of functions with precise parameter signatures. I'll use a helper type `ExtractParams` to recursively parse the path string and build a union of parameter names, then create a mapped type for the function parameters.

```typescript
type ExtractParams<T extends string> = T extends `${string}:${infer Param}/${infer Rest}`
  ? Param | ExtractParams<Rest>
  : T extends `${string}:${infer Param}`
    ? Param
    : never;

type MakeParamObject<T extends string> = ExtractParams<T> extends never
  ? {}
  : { [K in ExtractParams<T>]: string };

type InterpolationFn<T extends string> = T extends `${string}:${string}${string}`
  ? (params: MakeParamObject<T>) => string
  : () => string;

type DefineRoutes<Routes extends Record<string, string>> = {
  [K in keyof Routes]: InterpolationFn<Routes[K]>;
};

export function defineRoutes<Routes extends Record<string, string>>(routes: Routes): DefineRoutes<Routes> {
  const result = {} as any;

  for (const [name, path] of Object.entries(routes)) {
    result[name] = function(params?: Record<string, string>): string {
      return path.replace(/:([a-zA-Z0-9_]+)/g, (_, paramName) => {
        if (params && paramName in params) {
          return params[paramName];
        }
        throw new Error(`Missing required parameter: ${paramName}`);
      });
    } as any;
  }

  return result;
}
```

